{{ 'section-main-page.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- style -%}
  .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
    padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
    padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
      padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;
      padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
    }
  }
{%- endstyle -%}

<div class="page-width page-width--narrow section-{{ section.id }}-padding">
  <h1 class="main-page-title page-title h0{% if settings.animations_reveal_on_scroll %} scroll-trigger animate--fade-in{% endif %}">
    {{ page.title | escape }}
  </h1>
  <div class="rte{% if settings.animations_reveal_on_scroll %} scroll-trigger animate--slide-in{% endif %}">
    {{ page.content }}
  </div>
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  ==========================================================================
  ONE EVENING 26 :: EVENT LANDING PAGE
  Nothing above this comment was changed. This block is self-contained and
  uses no section settings, so the schema stays as it was.

  ALL CONTENT LIVES IN THE LIQUID BLOCK BELOW. Lists use "|" between items
  and "~" between the fields of one item, so everything stays editable in
  one place.

  Colour system (never hardcode a hex in the markup, use the tokens):
    Four colours, and nothing else:

    blue #07549A  THE DOMINANT. The page ground and most of what you see.
    acid #B63818  THE ORANGE RED. Stripes, badge boxes, CTAs, tiles, numbers.
    sun  #FFC425  THE GOLDEN YELLOW. Offsets, borders, secondary accents.
    on-dark #FFFFFF  white, for contrast.

    ink #01111F / forest #04355F / moss #0A4A85     deeper shades of the blue
    paper #FFFFFF / paper-dim #CFE0F0               light surfaces
    sun-lift #FFD65E  the lifted gold, hover only
    lime #FFC425  the gold again, used only as the hard offset shadow

    #B63818 is a DARK colour: its luminance is 0.13 against the blue's 0.09,
    so orange red type on the blue measures 1.3 to 1 and cannot be read.
    It is therefore a SURFACE here, never type on the blue, and the two
    layer treatment does the rest: the orange red block, the golden yellow
    offset behind it, white lettering on top. The one place orange red is
    type is the marquee, whose band is dark enough to carry it, and the 26,
    which takes the golden yellow offset for the same reason.

    Textures. Two, both inline SVG so nothing is fetched: a fractal smoke
    at 18 per cent (26 in the hero) and an eight point girih star lattice
    in gold line at 12 per cent over a 10 per cent wash. Both only ever
    darken the blue, so nothing they sit under loses contrast.
  ==========================================================================
{%- endcomment -%}

